    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I am Dr. Smith. Could you please tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S026",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. Smith. Well, um... it's just, I guess what finally pushed me to actually pick up the phone and make the appointment to come in today is that my eating has just been completely all over the place. And I mean, just totally unpredictable. It's so frustrating because, you know, I usually try to keep a somewhat normal routine, but lately... well, some weeks I'll sit down and I barely even touch my dinner. I just look at it and I have absolutely no interest, I just sort of push it around my plate and maybe take a bite or two, and that's it for the whole evening. \n\nBut then, it completely flips, and there are these other nights where... well, I wait until the house is totally quiet, after everyone’s gone to bed, and I just find myself standing in the middle of the kitchen. I don't even turn all the lights on or sit down at the table like a normal person. I just stand right there by the counter eating crackers, and just whatever sweets I can get my hands on. Like, I'll just stand there eating handfuls of cookies or whatever is left in the pantry. It's just so back and forth, going from nothing to just standing in the dark eating everything in sight, and I really didn't know what else to do because it's really starting to bother me...",
