    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you experienced periods like this before in your life, where you felt this same loss of interest and lack of energy, or is this the first time you've felt this way?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S024",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, I have. I mean, it's not the first time, not by a long shot. It's something that kind of... cycles around, I suppose you could say. I remember periods like this going back years, where I just go through these stretches—and they can last for weeks or even months—where everything just feels so different. \n\nLike, the whole house just feels gray and heavy, if that makes sense. It's not like the lights are actually dimmer, but it feels like they are. I'll just sit at the kitchen table, the one by the window where I usually like to watch the birds at the feeder, and I'll just sit there feeling completely empty. And the strange thing is, I'll be sitting there feeling this immense weight, this profound sadness almost, even though nothing terrible has happened that day. \n\nLike, nobody died, the bills are paid, the weather might even be perfectly fine outside, but I just have this sinking, heavy feeling in my chest. I remember one time, maybe three or four years ago, I sat at that same table for almost three hours just staring at the salt and pepper shakers. The salt shaker has a little chip on the bottom edge from when my husband dropped it in the sink, and I just stared at that chip, feeling like I couldn't possibly summon the energy to stand up and make a cup of tea. It just feels like all the air has been let out of the room, and I'm just existing in this heavy, gray space, waiting for it to pass, but not really believing it ever will. So, yes, it's definitely happened before, this same kind of empty, heavy feeling where nothing seems to matter.",
